<title>FRANCE: CYCLING-TOUR DE FRANCE 1997 STAGE WINNERS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-TOUR DE FRANCE 1997 STAGE WINNERS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is list of all the stage</p>
<p>winners on this year's Tour de France:</p>
<p>Prologue time trial (Rouen): Chris Boardman (Britain) GAN.</p>
<p>1 Rouen-Forges-les-Eaux: Mario Cipollini (Italy) Saeco.</p>
<p>2 St.Valery-en-Caux-Vire: Cipollini.</p>
<p>3 Vire-Plumelec: Erik Zabel (Germany) Telekom.</p>
<p>4 Plumelec-Le Puy-du-Fou: Nicola Minali (Italy) Batik.</p>
<p>5 Chantonnay-La Chatre: Cedric Vasseur (France) GAN.</p>
<p>6 Le Blanc-Marennes: Jeroen Blijlevens (Netherlands) TVM.</p>
<p>7 Marennes-Bordeaux: Zabel.</p>
<p>8 Sauternes-Pau: Zabel.</p>
<p>9 Pau-Loudenvielle: Laurent Brochard (France) Festina.</p>
<p>10 Luchon-Andorra: Jan Ullrich (Germany) Telekom.</p>
<p>11 Andorra-Perpignan: Laurent Desbiens (France) Cofidis.</p>
<p>12 St. Etienne time trial: Ullrich.</p>
<p>13 St. Etienne-l'Alpe d'Huez: Marco Pantani (Italy) Mercatone</p>
<p>Uno.</p>
<p>14 Le Bourg d'Oisans-Courchevel: Richard Virenque (France)</p>
<p>Festina.</p>
<p>15 Courchevel-Morzine: Pantani.</p>
<p>16 Morzine-Fribourg: Christophe Mengin (France) La Francaise</p>
<p>des Jeux.</p>
<p>17 Fribourg-Colmar: Neil Stephens (Australia) Festina.</p>
<p>18 Colmar-Montbeliard: Didier Rous (France) Festina.</p>
<p>19 Montbeliard-Dijon: Mario Traversoni (Italy) Mercatone Uno.</p>
<p>20 Disneyland (Paris) time trial: Abraham Olano (Spain)</p>
<p>Banesto.</p>
<p>21 Disneyland-Paris: Nicola Minali (Italy) Batik.</p>
</text>
